  {"date": "1996-12-30", "venue": "FleetCenter", "city": "Boston", "state": "MA", "gap": 3, "set": "2", "out": ">", "next": "Uncle Pen", "xprev": "Good Times Bad Times", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "1997-02-17", "venue": "Paradiso", "city": "Amsterdam", "state": "North Holland", "gap": 4, "set": "1", "out": ">", "prev": "Guyute", "next": "Billy Breathes", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "1997-07-01", "venue": "Paradiso", "city": "Amsterdam", "state": "North Holland", "gap": 22, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "An extremely well-played version kicks off the second set of very popular and highly rated show.", "out": ">", "prev": "Jam", "in": "->", "next": "Bathtub Gin", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "1997-07-26", "venue": "South Park Meadows", "city": "Austin", "state": "TX", "gap": 11, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "Bob Gullotti on a second drum set. Set II opener takes the typical \"Timber\" jam, extends it and cools it down a bit to a more mellow groove while maintaining a good rhythmic pulse. Never loses the dark \"Timber\" vibe.", "note": "Bob Gullotti on a second drum set.", "out": ">", "next": "David Bowie", "xprev": "Izabella", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "1997-08-11", "venue": "Deer Creek Music Center", "city": "Noblesville", "state": "IN", "gap": 9, "set": "2", "out": ">", "next": "Piper", "xprev": "Run Like an Antelope", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "1997-11-16", "venue": "McNichols Arena", "city": "Denver", "state": "CO", "gap": 6, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "Long intro to this big Set II opener featuring a jam that begins in typical \"Timber\" style, then shifts to delicate and serene major mode playing in the final minutes. Unfinished with a -> to \"Simple.\"", "out": "->", "next": "Simple", "xprev": "Hello My Baby", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "1997-11-28", "venue": "Worcester Centrum Centre", "city": "Worcester", "state": "MA", "gap": 6, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "Although it sticks with the \"Timber\" theme throughout, this is an excellent, well-played version. High quality SBD available on the \"Spreadsheet.\"", "out": ">", "next": "Limb By Limb", "xprev": "Rocky Top", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "1997-12-07", "venue": "Ervin J. Nutter Center, Wright State University", "city": "Dayton", "state": "OH", "gap": 6, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "\"Timber\" opens Set II for the 5th consecutive time in as many appearances. This excellent version has a slightly less dark and somber vibe than most and is an almost upbeat, contemplative piece.", "out": ">", "next": "Wolfman's Brother", "xprev": "Slave to the Traffic Light", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "1997-12-09", "venue": "Bryce Jordan Center, Penn State University", "city": "State College", "state": "PA", "gap": 0, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "Segue -> in from a 30 minute \"Simple,\" this version restores the jam to its typical place of darkness, and has an almost '95 psychedelic feel to it, with Fish kicking the percussion into heavier action.", "out": ">", "prev": "Simple", "in": "->", "next": "Contact", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "1997-12-31", "venue": "Madison Square Garden", "city": "New York", "state": "NY", "gap": 6, "set": "2", "out": ">", "next": "Mike's Song", "xprev": "Fire", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "1998-11-28", "venue": "Worcester Centrum Centre", "city": "Worcester", "state": "MA", "gap": 61, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "Much different than its '95 and '97 brethren, the jam in this version has that '98 swirly, ethereal tone, and Trey's guitar is far less shrill and dominant than in most earlier versions. Very well-played, especially by Page.", "out": ">", "prev": "Wolfman's Brother", "in": ">", "next": "Loving Cup", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "1999-07-17", "venue": "Oswego County Airport", "city": "Volney", "state": "NY", "gap": 17, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "Even further removed from the typical \"Timber\" jam than the '98 offering, this version is quite subdued and passively brooding. It gains momentum and power, but has none of the fury of earlier years. A high quality version nonetheless.", "prev": "Sneakin' Sally Thru the Alley", "in": ">", "next": "You Enjoy Myself", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "1999-12-29", "venue": "Big Cypress Seminole Indian Reservation", "city": "Big Cypress", "state": "FL", "gap": null, "set": "1", "prev": "Quinn the Eskimo (The Mighty Quinn)", "next": "Jam", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2000-07-14", "venue": "Polaris Amphitheater", "city": "Columbus", "state": "OH", "gap": 79, "set": "1", "jamchart": true, "jam": "More similar to pre-'97 versions with driving percussion and intense guitar work. A raging storm.", "prev": "Punch You in the Eye", "in": ">", "next": "Gotta Jibboo", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2000-09-30", "venue": "Thomas & Mack Center", "city": "Las Vegas", "state": "NV", "gap": 17, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "Big contrast to the 7/14/00 version as this jam has a more eerie, morose sentiment. An ominous cloud.", "next": "AC/DC Bag", "xprev": "Weekapaug Groove", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2003-07-29", "venue": "Post-Gazette Pavilion at Star Lake", "city": "Burgettstown", "state": "PA", "gap": 37, "set": "1", "jamchart": true, "jam": "Great segue -> in from \"Fee.\" This is one angry mule! Packs all the rage of the earliest versions. At 5:25, almost breaks free from \"Timber\" proper, but shortly returns to the fold.", "out": ">", "prev": "Fee", "in": "->", "next": "When the Circus Comes", "nb": 1},
